                <pb facs="0320" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.5045/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-13T14:00:00-05:00">December 13, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>113. All quiet. Damien Law and Medical School students still on strike; special
                    efforts have been made to induce medical students to return to their school but
                    so far without effect. Continuing efforts to start rural farm schools and
                    gradually all schools under the Service Technique.</p>
                <p>If conditions remain quiet I shall direct brigade commander to remove on December
                    16th the restriction regarding circulation after 9 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
